# Where the converter API lives.
#
# Leave this unset and the app talks to its own origin, which is how it is
# deployed: one reverse proxy in front of both the page and the API, so there is
# no CORS and no preflight. That is the default and it is the recommended one.
#
# Set it only when the API is served from somewhere else. Two things then have
# to be true of that deployment, or the app degrades quietly rather than
# breaking loudly:
#
#   1. The API must answer CORS for this origin. The request is preflighted,
#      because an XHR with an `upload` listener always is — and `upload` is how
#      the progress bar works.
#   2. It must EXPOSE `X-Request-Id` and `Content-Disposition`. A browser cannot
#      read a response header that CORS has not exposed, and the two headers
#      this client is built on are exactly those: without them a download is
#      named `converted.<ext>` and an error loses the reference number the user
#      is told to quote.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVERTER_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
